  "about": "Fictional demo data for the MeloMed hackathon starter. Maya Chen is a made-up college sophomore (biology major, climbs and runs), not a real person. tasks come from 2DooD, her to-do app. moods, entries and songs come from Nocturne, her journal app. Every date is written as if today is 2026-11-17. dayOffset is days from today (0 = today, -1 = yesterday, 4 = in four days). Mood is an automatic read of journal writing: valence runs from -1 (unpleasant) to 1 (pleasant), arousal from -1 (calm) to 1 (energized). The label \"apathy\" is how Nocturne marks tired days. Treat mood as a pattern for the person to look at, never a diagnosis. moods has one item per day that has a journal entry. Days with no entry are left out. Journal text is private and is not included.",
